## Change

`lib/request.js` — the `port` getter was parsing `this.headers.host ?? this.headers[':authority']` directly, bypassing the `host` getter. Under `trustProxy`, `host`/`hostname` come from `x-forwarded-host` while `port` came from the raw `Host` header, so the three could disagree.

It now parses `this.host`, and the regex is hoisted to a module-level `PORT_REG` instead of being recompiled on every access:

```js
port: {
  get () {
    const matches = PORT_REG.exec(this.host)
    if (matches === null || matches[1] === undefined) {
      return null
    }
    return parseInt(matches.groups.port.slice(1), 10)
  }
}
```

The parsing logic from #6603 is unchanged. `port` isn't overridden in `buildRequestWithTrustProxy`, so it inherits and picks up the trust-proxy `host` getter — the same way `hostname` already did.

